-- title:
--   Gauss's lemma for the j-expansion and its order
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $R \subseteq L$ a subring and $P \in L[X]$. Let [`ModularCurve.jqModC L`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) denote the Laurent series over $L$ given by the product of the Hahn series $q^{-1}$ (the monomial `HahnSeries.single (-1) 1`) with the power series obtained from [`ModularCurve.jNum`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L142) $= E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-\text{unit}}$ (the product of the cube of the Eisenstein series `eisenstein4` with `dedekindEtaUnitInv` in $\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$) by base change along $\mathbb{Z} \to L$; this is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, read in $L$. Assume that for every integer $n$ the $n$-th coefficient of the Laurent series $P(\mathrm{jqModC}\,L)$, obtained by evaluating $P$ at `jqModC L` through the $L$-algebra structure of `LaurentSeries L`, lies in $R$. The conclusion is twofold: first, every coefficient $P.\mathrm{coeff}\ i$, for $i \in \mathbb{N}$, lies in $R$; second, if $P \neq 0$ then the order (the least index of a nonzero coefficient) of $P(\mathrm{jqModC}\,L)$ equals $-\deg P$, where $\deg$ is `natDegree`.
--
--   This is the elementary Gauss-type descent statement for $q$-expansions: integrality of the coefficients of $P(j(q))$ forces integrality of the coefficients of $P$, with the order of vanishing computed exactly. It is used in the passage from integrality of $q$-expansions of modular forms to integrality over the polynomial ring generated by $j$, namely in [`ModularCurve.isIntegralElem_div_delta_pow_and_div_eisenstein4_pow_of_forall_qExpansion_slash_isIntegral`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isIntegralElem_div_delta_pow_and_div_eisenstein4_pow_of_forall_qExpansion_slash_isIntegral) and [`ModularCurve.isIntegralElem_div_delta_pow_and_div_eisenstein4_pow_of_isIntegralQExp_gamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isIntegralElem_div_delta_pow_and_div_eisenstein4_pow_of_isIntegralQExp_gamma1).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_forall_coeff_mem_of_forall_coeff_aeval_jqModC_mem.lean

